PROFIT-COST-1B legacy quality round-trip follow-up is complete on Draft PR #1015 at `2f50b41cb21c13881acb6a2b08f4088d02af26dc`.

Confirmed cause: the first compatibility read of complete legacy counters exported versioned financial-contract keys with null values, so a JSON round-trip made the next reader treat the result as an explicitly malformed new contract.

Minimal fix: resolved legacy/new counters and source metadata are now internal conversion state; only versioned fields actually present in the input are exported. Complete legacy totals, legacy envelopes, and old `_accounting_quality` output now remain complete after JSON round-trip. Explicit partial/null/wrong-version contracts still fail closed even with legacy zero counters or `financial_contract_present=false`; no missing-lines value is inferred from legacy.

Evidence:
- red-before: 3 expected failures, 6 controls passed;
- green focused matrix: 9 passed;
- green full affected suite: 136 passed (2 pre-existing Pydantic deprecation warnings);
- connected Salla-only amounts remain cost SAR 60 / net profit SAR 120;
- incomplete advertising and another missing accounting component remain blockers.

Changed only `backend/mezan_profit_engine.py`, `backend/campaign_ai_profit_accounting_gate.py`, `backend/tests/test_profit_cost_financial_completeness.py`, and `docs/fixes/PROFIT-COST-1B.md` in this follow-up. No amount/source-priority, estimator, historical snapshot/stored-cost, query/scan, provider/accounting write, resync/backfill, or Production/release action changed.

CI passed: Profit Cost Financial Completeness, Security Gate, both CodeQL jobs, Snapchat Settings Management V2, Qoyod Payment Freshness, Dashboard V2 Salla Ads Executive, and Dashboard V2 Ad FX And Payment Fees. Mezan Release Readiness remains failed at its clean-clone Release Intent A/B invariant; no Release Intent or release action was authorized or performed. PR #1015 remains Draft.

